[2mTwo layers: a reference model and a PID decide how much the car should rotate, a QP
allocator decides which wheels pay for it. The checks ask whether each layer does its
job, whether the tires were saturated enough for any of it to matter, and whether the
result survives the numbers it was built on.[0m

